course: dictionary
lesson: 16009
title: Variation: a change or difference
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Variation is a noun about change or difference. It can mean a change in amount or level, as in «There was a big variation in the temperature this week», where the temperature went up and down.
explain: It can also mean something slightly different from the usual form. «This is a variation on the game we played last year» means the game is nearly the same, but with a small change.
explain: In science, variation means the differences between living things of the same kind, such as height or eye colour. In maths, variation shows how much numbers spread out. Look at the words around it to choose the right meaning.
fact: Variation means a change or difference.
fact: A variation is something slightly different from the usual form, like a variation on a game.
fact: In science, variation means the differences between living things of the same kind, such as height or eye colour.
fact: In music, a variation is a new version of a tune.
fact: Useful phrases are «a variation on» and «variation in».
exercise: «There was a big variation in the temperature this week.» What does variation mean here? | *A change or difference in amount or level | A kind of weather | A type of thermometer | A map of the sky
exercise: «This is a variation on the game we played last year.» What does variation mean here? | A prize | A game for one player | *A slightly different version | The exact same game
exercise: In science, the differences between living things of the same kind are called what? | Vegetation | Vacation | Vibration | *Variation
test: The chef made a small ___ on the classic recipe by adding lemon. | *variation | vacation | vacuum | vibration
test: «The pianist played a new variation of the tune.» What does variation mean in this sentence? | A sad song | A loud noise | A piano lesson | *A new version of a tune
exam: In maths, what does variation show about a set of numbers? | The total of all the numbers | The name of the chart | The biggest number only | *How much the numbers spread out
